  "abstract": "Inspired by the current SOTA, this submission pivots to a new architectural family. It attempts to replicate the core concept of a low-rank factorization approach. The model encodes the 71,721 neurons into a 320-dimensional latent space, applies a simple temporal model (MLP) in this space, and then decodes the result back to the full neuron dimension. The hypothesis is that modeling dynamics in a compressed latent space is more efficient and powerful than the previous MoE architecture.",
  "submitted_tick": 52,
  "no_debugger": false,
  "cpu_only": false,
  "original_submission": {
    "content": "import flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nNUM_NEURONS = 71721\nINPUT_HORIZON = 4\nOUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'latent_dim': 320,  # k, based on Ariadne's tags\n        'mlp_hidden_dim': 128,\n    }\n\nclass LatentDynamicsModel(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    mlp_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x shape: (batch, 4, 71721)\n        \n        # Encoder: Project from neuron space to latent space\n        # (batch, 4, 71721) -> (batch, 4, 320)\n        latent_x = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name=\"encoder\")(x)\n\n        # Dynamics Model: Process sequence in latent space\n        # Flatten the time dimension for MLP processing\n        batch_size = latent_x.shape[0]\n        latent_flat = latent_x.reshape((batch_size, -1)) # (batch, 4 * 320)\n        \n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(latent_flat)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Predict the entire future sequence in the latent space\n        latent_y_flat = nn.Dense(features=OUTPUT_HORIZON * self.latent_dim)(y)\n        latent_y = latent_y_flat.reshape((batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, self.latent_dim))\n\n        # Decoder: Project from latent space back to neuron space\n        # (batch, 32, 320) -> (batch, 32, 71721)\n        output = nn.Dense(features=NUM_NEURONS, name=\"decoder\")(latent_y)\n        \n        return output\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = LatentDynamicsModel(\n            latent_dim=hparams.get('latent_dim'),\n            mlp_hidden_dim=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_dim')\n        )\n        self.mutable = []\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n",
